 "research_result": "Process judgment only, not a market result (research/simulation only; no experiment was run and no quantitative claim about any asset is made). The frontier-first focused-task selector is RETAINED: it produced six decisive, independently verified hypothesis-cell closures plus two qualification sweeps, eliminated the documented queue-sourced-objective selection defect, and keeps the durable queue aligned with the frontier's next action. The audit also found one real novelty-guard gap (cross-sectional momentum at 63 days is a one-parameter variant of the falsified CSRS cell at 20 days) and two durable-record gaps (missing activation-log sections for three activations; an unparseable frontier row on the only admitted positive cell), which are preserved as candidate tasks rather than fixed here. No controller redesign and no numeric reward score is proposed.",

